  "summary_en": "Montana statute limiting the admissibility of evidence obtained from unmanned aerial vehicles to cases with a search warrant, recognised warrant exceptions, or motor vehicle crash investigations on public roads. It also restricts use of such information in probable cause affidavits and defines UAVs.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "UAV-derived information is inadmissible unless obtained under a warrant, a recognised exception, or at a public roadway crash scene.",
   "UAV information cannot support a probable cause affidavit unless obtained under those circumstances.",
   "Defines UAV as an aircraft operated without direct human intervention on or within it, excluding satellites.",
   "Enacted 2013, amended 2019."
  ],
